% lps-converted-from: plan_generation.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program plan_generation.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 12.

the actions are:
    *a thing* walks *a second thing*; known as walk.
    *a thing* takes *a second thing*; known as take.
    *a thing* gives *a second thing* with *a third thing*; known as give.

the fluents are:
    *a thing* has *a second thing*.
    the at of *a thing* is *a second thing*; known as at.

the knowledge base plan_generation includes:

initially the at of john is home
    and the at of book is library
    and the at of mary is library
    and mary has book.

when a thing walks a second thing
then the at of the thing that is a third thing becomes the second thing.

when a thing takes a second thing
then the thing has the second thing.

when a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
then it is not the case that the thing has the third thing.

when a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
then the second thing has the third thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing walks a second thing
    and the at of the thing is the second thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing takes a second thing
    and the at of the thing is a third thing
    and it is not the case that the at of the second thing is the third thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing takes a second thing
    and a third thing has the second thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
    and it is not the case that the thing has the third thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
    and the at of the thing is a fourth thing
    and it is not the case that the at of the second thing is the fourth thing.

the goal is that john has book.

